### ADVANCED SCENARIOS
### ==================================================

### Scenario 1: Create Urgent Ticket with Immediate Assignment
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}
X-Tenant: acme

{
  "subject": "Server Down - Production Environment",
  "description": "Production server is completely down. All customers unable to access the system. Need immediate attention.",
  "contactId": "contact-1-acme",
  "assigneeId": "user-1-acme",
  "priority": "URGENT",
  "category": "BUG",
  "source": "PHONE",
  "slaDeadline": "2025-01-07T08:00:00Z",
  "tags": ["critical", "server", "production", "downtime"]
}

### Scenario 2: Bulk Filter - All Open High Priority Technical Support Tickets Past SLA
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets?status=OPEN&priority=HIGH&category=TECHNICAL_SUPPORT&slaPast=true&sortBy=slaDeadline&sortOrder=asc
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}
X-Tenant: acme

### Scenario 3: Get Statistics for Support Manager Dashboard
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/stats?startDate=2025-01-01&endDate=2025-01-31
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}
X-Tenant: acme

### Scenario 4: Track Ticket Through Complete Lifecycle
# Create ticket
# @name lifecycleTicket
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}
X-Tenant: acme

{
  "subject": "Integration Issue with Third-Party API",
  "description": "Customer reports integration with Salesforce API is failing. Getting 401 authentication errors.",
  "contactId": "contact-2-acme",
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "category": "TECHNICAL_SUPPORT",
  "source": "EMAIL",
  "slaDeadline": "2025-01-09T17:00:00Z",
  "tags": ["integration", "salesforce", "api"]
}

###
# Assign ticket
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/{{lifecycleTicket.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}
X-Tenant: acme

{
  "assigneeId": "user-2-acme"
}

###
# Start working
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/{{lifecycleTicket.response.body.id}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}
X-Tenant: acme

{
  "status": "IN_PROGRESS"
}

###
# Waiting for customer response
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/{{lifecycleTicket.response.body.id}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}
X-Tenant: acme

{
  "status": "PENDING"
}

###
# Continue working after customer reply
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/{{lifecycleTicket.response.body.id}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}
X-Tenant: acme

{
  "status": "IN_PROGRESS"
}

###
# Mark as resolved
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/{{lifecycleTicket.response.body.id}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}
X-Tenant: acme

{
  "status": "RESOLVED"
}

###
# Close ticket
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/{{lifecycleTicket.response.body.id}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}
X-Tenant: acme

{
  "status": "CLOSED"
}

###
# Verify final state with all timestamps
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/{{lifecycleTicket.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}
X-Tenant: acme

### ==================================================
### END OF TESTS
